         0.41.0 — fuaran#1075. MINOR, and the reasoning is on the SEMANTICS
         axis rather than the surface one: `Binding.State.defaultValue` stops
         being a per-reader fallback and SEEDS its slot, so a document that
         decoded yesterday renders a different value today wherever two readers
         share a key. No wire byte moves and no fixture payload changes. The
         additive surface rides along (two `BindingUse` cases, two
         `StateKeyFacts` fields, two `PreEmitDefect` cases → FUARAN106 /
         FUARAN107, `BindingWalk.stateSeeds`, `Render.withStateSeeds`), each a
         construction-site break on the 0.36.0 / 0.39.0 / 0.40.0 precedent.
         Admitted by operator ruling under the shared-data-source charter's own
         reopening condition. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change — 0.41.0". -->
