    <!-- 0.48.0 (Phase 1144) — the typed-`Actor` DAG fold, a MAJOR-axis wire
         event on `Fuaran.UI.OpStream.Dag.*`. `DagOpRecord.UserId: string`
         becomes `Actor: Actor`, the content-address pre-image's `"userId"`
         member becomes `"actor":<Actor.encode>`, and the canonical wire record
         carries `"actor"` (Ordinal-first) in place of the trailing `"userId"`.
         Because Phase 408 had already folded attribution INTO the address,
         typing it RE-ADDRESSES EVERY DAG NODE: pre-1144 DAG content addresses
         do not carry forward and there is no in-place upgrade for a persisted
         DAG. This takes its own version slot rather than riding the in-flight
         0.47.0 — that slot carries four ADDITIVE changes, and a reader
         scanning the history for the release that moved the DAG wire must not
         have to find it inside a minor that otherwise reads as growth.
         Pre-1.0, so the major axis still rides a minor bump (STABILITY.md §
         "the semver rules take effect from 1.0.0"). See STABILITY.md "Recorded
         breaking change — 0.48.0" and
         docs/migrations/1144-typed-actor-dag-fold.md. -->
    <!-- 0.49.0 (Phase 1154) — the VB XML dialect's state-binding spelling, and
         the `Binding.State(key)` overload on `Fuaran.UI.CSharp` it drives.
         Both are additive on the public surface and neither changes a byte any
         shipped tree encodes to, so a minor on the pre-1.0 axis. It takes its
         own slot rather than riding the in-flight 0.48.0 for the mirror of the
         reason that slot was cut: 0.48.0's headline is a BREAKING DAG
         re-address, and an additive authoring-surface change must not be
         findable only inside it. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change — 0.49.0,
         the VB state-binding spelling". -->
    <!-- 0.50.0 (Phase 1112) — the node-level `Tooltip` trait. BREAKING for
         record-literal construction of `Node` (a new field is FS0764, an ERROR,
         at every full-literal site), additive on the wire. It takes its own
         slot rather than riding 0.49.0 for that slot's own stated reason: 0.49.0
         is an ADDITIVE authoring-surface change, and a reader adopting it must
         not discover a source-breaking record widening inside it. Pre-1.0, so
         the major axis still rides a minor bump. See STABILITY.md "Recorded
         change — 0.50.0, the node-level `Tooltip` trait". -->
    <!-- 0.51.0 (Phase 1113) — `FormFieldKind.Combobox`, the typeahead /
         autocomplete control. Additive: a new DU case leaves every existing
         match compiling and raises FS0025 only where one is exhaustive, which
         is the correct signal. Wire-additive too — no shipped document's bytes
         move, and `allowFreeText` omits at `false` so the shortest combobox is
         the constrained one. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change — 0.51.0,
         `FormFieldKind.Combobox`". -->
    <!-- 0.52.0 (Phase 1151) — the fragment-expansion memo. Additive on every
         axis: a new module `Fuaran.UI.Renderer.FragmentExpansion` in
         Fuaran.UI.Renderer.Core and two new functions on `Render`. No existing
         signature changes, `RenderContext` is untouched, and NOTHING on the wire
         moves — a memo is invisible there. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change —
         0.52.0, the fragment-expansion memo". -->
    <!-- 0.53.0 (Phase 742) - `read.nodeJson` on the DevTools relay, which advances
         the relay profile to `relay@1.3`. Outside the wire format entirely: no
         shipped document's bytes move and the typed tree is untouched. Source-
         breaking in one narrow place - `Relay.RelaySurface` gains a field, so a
         full-literal construction of that record is FS0764; `Relay.surfaceOf`
         (the supported route) fills it. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change -
         0.53.0, `read.nodeJson` on the DevTools relay". -->
    <!-- 0.54.0 (Phase 1115) - `FileUpload` drop target + paste ingestion. Wire-
         additive: two bool members on `FileUploadSpec`, both omitted at `false`,
         so no shipped document's bytes move and every upload written before this
         release decodes to the control it always was. Source-breaking in one
         narrow place - the record gains fields, so a full-literal construction is
         FS0764; `Defaults.fileUpload` fills both, which is why the supported
         `{ Defaults.fileUpload with ... }` route is unaffected. Its own slot
         rather than riding 0.53.0 for the reason 1112 recorded: 0.53.0's headline
         is a relay-profile advance, and a reader adopting THAT number should not
         discover a wire-vocabulary addition inside it. See STABILITY.md "Recorded
         change - 0.54.0, `FileUpload` drop target and paste ingestion". -->
    <!-- 0.56.0 (Phase 1181) - the generated structural layer is regenerated from
         THIS repo's own `idl.json` + `support.json` now, and a vocabulary loaded
         from bytes declares its kinds in Ordinal order rather than the authored
         family order. So `src/Fuaran.UI/Generated.fs` is REORDERED: the emitted
         content is byte-for-byte what it was (identical file length, identical
         line multiset bar the two recursion-group head markers that swap), but
         `NodeKind`'s 42 cases and the 313 type declarations are now Ordinal.
         Nothing on the wire moves - the encoder emits by case NAME - and no
         exhaustive `match` breaks, because the case SET is unchanged. What does
         move is the compiled DU tag ordinal, which is binary contract, and a
         contract change never rides a same-version repack. See STABILITY.md
         "Recorded change - 0.56.0, the generated layer regenerates in-process". -->
    <!-- 0.58.0 (Phase 1179) - `Fuaran.UI.ServerDriven` gains the live-Transform
         incremental seam: `LiveTransformStore`, `LiveTransformEvaluation` and the
         `LiveTransform` module beside them. Purely additive and in the shape that
         carries no FS0764 risk at all - three NEW surfaces, no existing type
         gaining a member, no signature moved, nothing on the wire. 0.57.0 was
         taken concurrently by Phase 1098; this is the next slot rather than a
         re-pack of it. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change - 0.58.0, the
         live-Transform incremental seam". -->
    <!-- 0.59.0 (Phase 1472) - `SemanticStyle` gains `direction`, the declared base
         direction of one authored value. Additive on the wire and omitted at its
         `Auto` default, so every pre-1472 document is byte-identical; but a RECORD
         gains a member, which is FS0764 at every full-literal construction site,
         so it is a version of its own and never a re-pack. 0.58.0 was taken
         concurrently by Phase 1179; this is the next slot. See STABILITY.md
         "Recorded change - 0.59.0, `SemanticStyle.direction`". -->
    <!-- 0.61.0 (Phase 1120) - `NodeKind.Tree`, recursive disclosure with tree
         semantics. A new NodeKind CASE, which is source-breaking at every
         exhaustive match over the DU - the FormFieldKind.DateRange precedent -
         so it rides a minor bump and never a re-pack. Additive on the wire:
         nothing is removed and every pre-1120 document encodes and decodes to
         byte-identical bytes. 0.60.0 was taken by Phase 1473; this is the next
         slot. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change - 0.61.0, `NodeKind.Tree`". -->
    <!-- 0.64.0 (Phase 1124) - `Action.Print`, the vocabulary's first PAYLOAD-FREE
         case, plus `ActionDescriptor.Print`, `StructuralQuery.Act.Print` and
         `ClientEffect.Print` riding with it. Additive on the wire: nothing is
         removed and every pre-1124 document encodes and decodes to byte-identical
         bytes. But a new DU case is source-breaking at every exhaustive match -
         the FormFieldKind.DateRange precedent (0.7.0) - so it rides a minor bump
         and never a re-pack. `IFuaranRuntime` is deliberately UNCHANGED: the
         effect is renderer-native on the `Action.CommitLocal` precedent, so no
         existing implementer gains a member. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change -
         0.64.0, `Action.Print` and the print stylesheet". -->
    <!-- fuaran#1116 (0.68.0) - `FileUploadSpec.Capture : CaptureSource option`,
         plus the new closed two-case enum it names. Additive on the wire: the
         member is absent at `None`, so every upload document written before this
         release encodes to byte-identical bytes. Source-breaking ONLY at a
         full-literal `FileUploadSpec` construction (FS0764), which
         `Defaults.fileUpload` fills - and NOT exhaustiveness-breaking, because
         `CaptureSource` is a new type nothing matches on yet. It rides a minor
         bump rather than a re-pack for the reason every entry above does: a
         re-packed slot swaps the contract under a consumer whose NuGet cache
         still serves the old bits. See STABILITY.md "Recorded change - 0.68.0,
         the media-capture upload field". -->
    <!-- fuaran#1485 (0.71.0) - the op-stream sinks' compare-and-append and keyed
         append. ADDITIVE. `Fuaran.UI.OpStream.Abstractions` gains `AppendReceipt`,
         `CasAppendOutcome`, `KeyedAppendOutcome` and two OPTIONAL extension
         interfaces - `IOpStreamCasSink<'Msg>` / `IOpStreamKeyedSink<'Msg>` - on the
         `IOpStreamCheckpointSink` shape: they INHERIT `IOpStreamSink<'Msg>` rather
         than widening it, so an existing implementer of the base compiles unchanged.
         `Fuaran.UI.OpStream.Replay` gains `ApplyPersist.applyWithSinksKeyed`. Both
         shipped stores implement both; the SQLite store gains an `op_invocation`
         side table created by `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` on open, so an existing
         database migrates by being opened and no `op_stream` row is rewritten. No
         existing member changed signature, no DU gained a case and no record gained
         a field, so nothing here is source-breaking. It rides a minor bump rather
         than a re-pack for the reason every entry above does: a re-packed slot swaps
         the contract under a consumer whose NuGet cache still serves the old bits.
         See STABILITY.md "Recorded change - 0.71.0, the op-stream sinks'
         compare-and-append and keyed append". -->
    <Version>0.74.0</Version>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Package metadata for the published Fuaran.UI.* packages (nuget.org
       + the fuaran-ui GitHub Packages feed). The repo is Apache-2.0;
       PackageLicenseExpression is the single licence channel — do not set
       PackageLicenseFile anywhere (the two are mutually exclusive:
       NU5033). -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/fuaran-ui/fuaran-dotnet</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/fuaran-ui/fuaran-dotnet</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- CI restores from an empty local feed and falls through to nuget.org, so a package version
         that exists only in a machine-local feed is NU1102 here. -->
    <FuaranRestorePath>public</FuaranRestorePath>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
